WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.000
1916. From Tokyo, Zhao Shen telegraphs in cipher to the insurgents of southern China.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.160
6 June: death of Yuan Shikai, the would-be emperor.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.400
23 June, G0 channel to Zhaoqing: 11,000 Japanese rifles have arrived at Moji.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.280
14 July: the Military Affairs Council dissolves itself.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.800
12 July: a message to Shanghai, the future held-out test of the decipherment.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.680
19 July: the same message on both channels. "The attitude of the Japanese has suddenly changed."

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.520
September, Y0 channel to Yunnan: six military aircraft, eight wireless sets.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.200
30 September: "otherwise our credit would be ruined".

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.440
October: commemorative medals, a loan at 8% without guarantee.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.340
5 November: "I return south on the 10th."

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.560
8 November: General Cai E dies at Fukuoka. Zhao Shen announces it to Yunnan.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.280
17 telegrams of 1916 deciphered, on two channels. Those of 1917 still resist.

